Practical No. 13
Request Validation using Bean Validation (@Valid) with RestController
Textbook Reference: Chapter 6 — Building RESTful Microservices
Objective
Validate incoming JSON payloads declaratively using Jakarta Bean Validation annotations (@NotBlank,
@Email, @Min) combined with @Valid on the controller method. Built with Spring Boot, Spring Data JPA,
Maven, and an embedded H2 database.
Project Setup Summary
Build tool: Maven | Framework: Spring Boot | Database: H2 (in-memory) | Base package:
com.example.customerapi
Package layout: entity, repository, controller.
The class list marks Customer as “@Entity / DTO, reused”, so — as in the task instructions — the JPA entity itself
carries the validation annotations and is used directly as the request/response body, with no separate DTO/mapper
layer for this practical.
